---
// The homepage's recording: the agent harness, playing beside the introduction. The text inside the
// "fallback" slot is what a reader sees when scripts are off, and `frame` is the screen of the recording
// at 13 seconds (the poster), replayed from harness-demo.cast.
import CastPlayer from './CastPlayer.astro';

const source = 'https://github.com/ayeshLK/module-termui/tree/main/examples/agent-harness';
const frame = `❯ fix the bug in the handler
I'll start by looking at where the request is handled.
● Read(src/handler.bal)
  ⎿  142 lines
● Grep("nil" in src/)
  ⎿  3 matches in 2 files
Found it. parseBody returns () for an empty payload and the caller dereferences it without
checking. Here is the fix:
    function parseBody(http:Request req) returns json|error {
        json|error body = req.getJsonPayload();
        if body is error {
            return {};   // treat an empty payload as an empty object
        }
        return body;
    }
Let me apply that change.
⠴ Running Edit(src/handler.bal)… (7s · ↓ 96 tokens · esc to interrupt)
❯ █
  dummy-agent-1 · 96 tokens · /help for commands · ctrl+d to quit
? Allow Edit(src/handler.bal)? (y/N)`;
---

<CastPlayer
	cast="harness-demo.cast"
	cols={92}
	rows={26}
	poster="npt:0:13"
	autoplay
	loop
	caption={`An agent harness built with termui, recorded from the real program. <a href="${source}">See its source.</a>`}
>
	<Fragment slot="fallback">
		<p>What the recording shows, in order:</p>
		<ol>
			<li>The harness starts with a prompt, and you type <code>fix the bug in the handler</code>.</li>
			<li>
				A spinner and a status line (elapsed time, tokens, how to interrupt) stay at the bottom while the
				answer streams in above them.
			</li>
			<li>
				Each tool call (<code>Read</code>, <code>Grep</code>) and each paragraph of the answer, once
				finished, is written into the terminal's normal scrollback.
			</li>
			<li>
				Before <code>Edit</code> and again before <code>Bash(bal test)</code>, the program asks for approval
				and waits for <code>y</code> or <code>n</code>.
			</li>
			<li>When the answer is complete the prompt comes back. After you quit, the whole session stays in the scrollback.</li>
		</ol>
		<p>The screen at the first approval prompt:</p>
		<pre><code set:text={frame} /></pre>
		<p>The source is in <a href={source}><code>examples/agent-harness</code></a>.</p>
	</Fragment>
</CastPlayer>
